19. Remove Nth Node From End of List

🚀 Optimal Method — One Pass (Fast & Slow Pointer)
⭐ Main Idea
👉 We create a gap of n nodes between two pointers. FAST ---- n nodes ahead ---- SLOW

When FAST reaches the end… 👉 SLOW will be standing just before the node we must delete.
That is the entire trick.

🔥 MOST IMPORTANT TRICK — Use a Dummy Node
Why beginners struggle: Deleting the head is annoying.
Example: 1 → 2 → 3         n = 3
You must delete 1. But there is no node before it!

Solution:

Create a fake node:  dummy → 1 → 2 → 3
Now EVEN the head has a previous node 😄   Always use dummy in linked list deletion problems.

✅ Step-by-Step Visualization

Example:
head = 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5        n = 2
We must delete 4.

✅ Step 1 — Setup pointers
dummy → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5
 ^ 
slow, fast both start here

✅ Step 2 — Move FAST first
Move it n+1 steps.
Why n+1?
Because we want:
👉 slow to stop BEFORE the node to delete.

Let’s move:
Move 1 → fast at 1
Move 2 → fast at 2
Move 3 → fast at 3

Now the gap is correct.
slow at dummy
fast at 3

Distance between them = 3 nodes.

✅ Step 3 — Move BOTH together

Now move one step at a time:

Move 1:
slow → 1
fast → 4

Move 2:
slow → 2
fast → 5

Move 3:
slow → 3
fast → null (end!)

STOP.

✅ Step 4 — Delete Node

Currently:
slow → 3
slow.next → 4   ❌ delete this

Just do:
slow.next = slow.next.next;

Now list becomes:

1 → 2 → 3 → 5

DONE ✅

🧠 Why This Works (Important Intuition)

Because FAST was n steps ahead…

When FAST travels the remaining distance to reach NULL…

SLOW automatically lands at:

👉 node_before_target

No counting needed.
No second traversal.

Just pointer magic 🪄

Code:

/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * public class ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode next;
 *     ListNode() {}
 *     ListNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     ListNode(int val, ListNode next) { this.val = val; this.next = next; }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public ListNode removeNthFromEnd(ListNode head, int n) {
        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);
        dummy.next=head;

        ListNode slow = dummy;
        ListNode fast = dummy;

        for(int i=0;i<n+1;i++){
            fast=fast.next;
        }

        while(fast!=null){
            slow=slow.next;
            fast=fast.next;
        }

        slow.next=slow.next.next;

        return dummy.next;
    }
}
